## Context

Twentieth run. Five journal entries, four tasks. Major themes: GPX4-ILC2 ferroptosis validated (Cell Mol Immunol 2026), biopsy microbiome anti-TNF classifier AUC 0.90, PALI-2108 ECCO RNA-seq, host-microbiome metabolic modeling, TL1A pipeline acceleration.

### Journal entries created
- #2537: GPX4-dependent ferroptosis governs ILC2 homeostasis in colitis (Liu et al., Cell Mol Immunol 2026). ILC2-specific susceptibility confirmed; ILC3s not susceptible. Plus 4 supporting papers: Panx1/macrophage ferroptosis (6th compartment), METTL14/m6A/GPX4, A. muciniphila→GPX4 upregulation, shikonin/GPX4 barrier function.
- #2538: Colonic biopsy 16S predicts anti-TNF response AUC 0.90 (Zafeiropoulou et al., Front Cell Infect Microbiol 2026). 125 CD patients. M. gnavus=non-response, Blautia=response. Converges with bile acid/Bifidobacterium axis (#2531).
- #2539: PALI-2108 ECCO 2026 RNA-seq from UC biopsies. 186 fibrosis/stricture genes normalized. JAK-STAT/NF-κB/TNF-α/MAPK/TGF-β suppressed. FSCD-specific topline still pending. Phase 2 IND planned H1 2026.
- #2540: Host-microbiome metabolic modeling (Taubenheim et al., Nat Comms 2025). Tryptophan→NAD depletion, glutathione disruption. Multi-level dysregulation across microbiome/transcriptome/metabolome.
- #2541: TL1A pipeline update. Duvakitug Phase 3 + $400M Blackstone. Tulisokibart Phase 2a Lancet publication + expanded to 3 additional autoimmune indications. Ontunisertib ECCO 2026 + Phase 2b H2 2026.

### Tasks created
- #1657 (research_director, P2): Integrate ILC2-specific ferroptosis validation + Panx1 macrophage 6th compartment into convergence model
- #1658 (research_director, P2): Evaluate biopsy microbiome anti-TNF classifier for multi-modal integration
- #1659 (data_curator, P3): Check Zafeiropoulou et al. 16S biopsy data availability (125 CD patients)
- #1660 (research_director, P3): Evaluate tryptophan-NAD and glutathione axes for targeted metabolite annotation

### Key highlights for next run
- GPX4-ILC2 ferroptosis now experimentally validated (Liu et al. CMI 2026). Convergence model now has 6 compartments: epithelial, ILC2, fibroblast, macrophage (Panx1), anti-TNF non-responder signature, post-op recurrence. Plus ACSL4, microbiome (A. muciniphila), and epigenetic (METTL14/m6A) regulatory layers.
- Biopsy microbiome anti-TNF prediction (AUC 0.90): M. gnavus/Blautia axis. Check data availability. Multi-modal classifier opportunity (transcriptomic + biopsy microbiome + bile acid).
- PALI-2108 FSCD topline: still not released as of Mar 30. Was expected Q1 2026. Check next run. Phase 2 IND planned H1 2026.
- DDW 2026: May 2-5 Chicago. Late-breaking abstract submissions closed Mar 18. Abstracts should be publicly searchable by late April. Mine after conference.
- TL1A race intensifying: duvakitug Phase 3 + $400M Blackstone (Mar 2026), tulisokibart ARES-CD Phase 3 recruiting. Both have anti-fibrotic potential relevant to fibrosis drug repurposing benchmarking.
- GALAXI biopsy transcriptomics: still not released despite Phase 3 Lancet publication. Monitor for substudy publications.
- Ontunisertib: STENOVA Phase 2a presented ECCO 2026 (OP20). Phase 2b planned H2 2026. Agomab filed US IPO.
- Prior monitoring items still pending: SPARC IBD metabolomics (#1065), ARES-CD CDx genotype panel, anti-TNF serum proteomics/HLA-DQB1*03:01 biomarkers, Verstockt GPX4 data deposition check (#1265), Kong/Washburn GEO data deposition.
- VICTRIVA (upadacitinib+vedolizumab) dual-targeted therapy: still recruiting.
- Next: DDW 2026 abstract mining (after May 2-5), PALI-2108 FSCD topline, GALAXI biopsy substudies, ontunisertib Phase 2b initiation, duvakitug/tulisokibart Phase 3 updates, check Liu et al. ILC2-GPX4 dataset deposition, Zafeiropoulou 16S data availability.
